'''ZedScripts''' is a [[wikipedia:Language Server Protocol|language server protocol (LSP)]] for the [[Scripts]] syntax. It parses the script files in one or more workspaces and provided libraries in configuration files to tokenize and create tree structures of your scripts to finally provide features like syntax highlighting, code completion, and diagnostics.

It allows [[Wikipedia:Integrated development environment|IDE]]s such as [[Visual Studio Code]], [[IntelliJ IDEA]] or even [[wikipedia:Vim (text editor)|Vim]] to interact with the script files more intelligently, providing real-time feedback and assistance during development.

== Usage ==
{{Note|You can find detailed documentation on the [[github:PZ-Wiki-Modding/ZedScripts-LSP|ZedScripts-LSP GitHub page]].}}

The easiest method to use it is by installing [[Visual Studio Code]] and then installing the [https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=SimKDT.ZedScripts “ZedScripts” extension by SimKDT]. Script files should automatically get detected as ''ZedScripts'' files as long as they follow a correct [[Mod structure|modding structure]].

